# Risk Rules DSL

All competency risk rules must conform to the corporate L&D JSON DSL schema. Rules are stored in the `rules-db` and loaded by the Risk Engine Service at runtime.

## Required fields

```json
{
  "ruleId": "RISK_CORP_XXX",
  "ruleName": "Human-readable name",
  "description": "Business intent for L&D admins and auditors",
  "severity": "CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW",
  "priority": 10,
  "enabled": true,
  "version": "1.0",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-01-01",
  "conditions": {
    "operator": "AND|OR",
    "criteria": [
      { "metric": "attendance_percentage", "period": "30_days", "operator": "less_than", "value": 75 }
    ]
  },
  "actions": {
    "setRiskLevel": "HIGH",
    "riskTag": ["ATTENDANCE_RISK"],
    "alert": ["employee", "manager", "ld_admin"],
    "intervention": ["remedial_training"],
    "requireHumanReview": false
  }
}
```

## Human-review requirement

`requireHumanReview` **must be `true`** for any rule with `severity: CRITICAL` or `severity: HIGH`. This is mandatory for GDPR Art.22, CCPA, and DPDP automated-profiling compliance. A Risk Review record must be created and acknowledged by a Trainer or L&D Manager before employee notifications are dispatched.

## Metric names

Use only the approved metric names from `02-database.md`: `attendance_percentage`, `assessment_score`, `consecutive_assessment_failures`, `score_trend_decline_percent`, `milestone_status`, `days_milestone_overdue`, `days_to_compliance_deadline`, `days_since_intervention_closed`, `post_intervention_score_improved`, `certification_days_to_expiry`.

## Versioning

Every rule change increments `version`. Old versions are retained in `risk_rule_versions` for audit. Never delete a rule — set `enabled: false` and record an `effectiveTo` date.
